学んでしまった。
She learned something bad.

1066
00:54:18,580 --> 00:54:21,080
シャラップお願いシャラップ！
Shut up, please, shut up!

1067
00:54:21,580 --> 00:54:26,080
はい。まあ「ツクツクボウシ」か「ツクツクホウシ」、どっちでもオッケー。
Yes. Well, either "Tsukutsukuboushi" or "Tsukutsukuhoushi" is okay.

1068
00:54:26,580 --> 00:54:30,080
ツクツクホウシ？／どっちでもオッケーで。
Tsukutsukuhoushi? / Either one is fine.

1069
00:54:30,080 --> 00:54:33,580
へえー、ツクツクボース。／となっております。
Huh, Tsukutsukuboushi. / That is the answer.

1070
00:54:34,080 --> 00:54:37,080
はい。ちょっとね、これセミは難しいですねー。
Yes. Cicadas are a bit tricky, aren't they?

1071
00:54:37,080 --> 00:54:38,080
Wow.

1072
00:54:38,080 --> 00:54:40,580
へえー、セミの種類とかは関係ないんですか？
Huh, so the species of cicada doesn't matter?

1073
00:54:40,580 --> 00:54:44,580
あ、これは「ツクツクボウシ」っていうセミの鳴き声ですね、今のは。
Oh, this one was the call of a cicada species called "Tsukutsukuboushi".

1074
00:54:44,580 --> 00:54:46,080
あ、種類？
Oh, the species?

1075
00:54:46,080 --> 00:54:49,580
そう、種類も「ツクツクボウシ」っていう名前のセミ。
Yes, the species itself is a cicada named "Tsukutsukuboushi".

1076
00:54:49,580 --> 00:54:51,080
へえー。
Huh.

1077
00:54:51,080 --> 00:54:54,580
ちなみに他にも、さっきのがミンミンゼミだったでしょ？
By the way, the previous one was the Minminzemi, right?

1078
00:54:54,580 --> 00:54:59,080
アブラゼミっていうのが、あのジジがさっき言ってた「ジジジジジジジ」って鳴くのがアブラ...
And the Aburazemi is the one that cries "Ji-ji-ji-ji-ji" like Gigi said earlier...

1079
00:55:00,088 --> 00:55:01,388
セミだったり
...like cicadas.

1080
00:55:01,388 --> 00:55:03,088
アブラゼミ。/ アブラゼミ、はい。
A large brown cicada. / A large brown cicada, yes.

1081
00:55:03,088 --> 00:55:05,588
日本人だったら...
If you're Japanese...

1082
00:55:05,588 --> 00:55:09,088
セミの声を聞くだけで、何のセミか分かります。
just by hearing a cicada chirp, you can tell what kind it is.

1083
00:55:09,388 --> 00:55:11,788
えー！ Wow! / Wow.
Huh?! / Wow! / Wow.

1084
00:55:12,088 --> 00:55:14,588
They can differentiate what kind of...

1085
00:55:14,588 --> 00:55:17,588
...cicada it is depending on what it sounds like?

1086
00:55:17,588 --> 00:55:19,688
There's different enchiladas?

1087
00:55:19,688 --> 00:55:23,888
Enchila— Yeah, so what we heard were two different enchiladas, Gigi.

1088
00:55:24,088 --> 00:55:27,288
So you're saying that there is an enchilada that says "ji-ji"?

1089
00:55:27,288 --> 00:55:29,088
Yeah, there is. / Yeah, there is.

1090
00:55:29,088 --> 00:55:32,488
え、3種類って何の名前だったっけ？
Wait, what were the names of those 3 kinds?

1091
00:55:32,488 --> 00:55:36,088
えーと、「ジジジ」はアブラゼミですね。
Um, "ji-ji-ji" is the large brown cicada.

1092
00:55:36,088 --> 00:55:38,288
アブラゼミ！ / はい。
Aburazemi! / Yes.

1093
00:55:38,288 --> 00:55:40,088
アブラゼミ... / 茶色のやつ？
Aburazemi... / The brown one?

1094
00:55:40,088 --> 00:55:42,288
アブラゼミ... / アブラゼミ。/ Yes.
Aburazemi... / Aburazemi. / Yes.

1095
00:55:42,288 --> 00:55:44,288
アブラゼミ、はい。/ After together?
Aburazemi, yes. / After together?

1096
00:55:44,288 --> 00:55:46,888
A large brown cicada. Mm.

1097
00:55:46,888 --> 00:55:50,588
はい。/ Large brown cicada goes...
